From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] P7 task 7: FAQ-suggestion strip with a one-click Apply

Adds the missing consumer for `FAQ_SUGGESTION_POPUP_ENABLED`: a small,
dismissible strip in the reply composer's top panel (the same file 0002 and
0055 already extend) that shows the single best-matching FAQ suggestion for
the conversation's latest customer message, with an "Apply" button.

WHY THIS DOES NOT FIGHT THE IFRAME SANDBOX. The existing agent-assist FAQ
panel (`backend/apps/chatwoot-agent-app/`) is a cross-origin Chatwoot
Dashboard App iframe with no postMessage API for writing into the reply
editor -- that limitation is real and is documented at length in that app's
README, which this patch does NOT change or contradict. This patch instead
reuses the mechanism 0002 already built for exactly this problem: the
`protonAssistResult` event that `ReplyTopPanel.vue` already emits and
`ReplyBox.vue` already handles (`onProtonAssistResult`), which runs inside
Chatwoot's own frontend bundle rather than a sandboxed iframe, so it can set
`this.message` directly. Applying a suggestion here calls the exact same
`emit('protonAssistResult', { text, mode: 'reply' })` the three existing
Copilot actions call -- no new bridge, no new event, and (this is the
regression this patch must not cause) no change whatsoever to those three
actions' own call of that same emit. The iframe path is superseded for this
one feature, not replaced in general: the side panel keeps working exactly
as before for agents who prefer to browse rather than accept a suggestion.

WHAT IT FETCHES. `GET /kb/suggest?q=<latest customer message>&limit=1`
(`kb_suggest_router.py`, unchanged by this patch) is called directly with
`fetch()` -- not through `callAssist()`, which only knows `/assist/*` -- via
`backendUrl`, now also destructured off `useProtonConfig()` alongside the
`hasFeature` it already read. Confidence gating relies on a fact already
true of that endpoint's response shape: only `live_faq` hits carry a numeric
`score` (Vertex hits never do), so `FAQ_SUGGESTION_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD`
(0.75) rejects anything without a `score` by construction -- there is no
separate "is this a Vertex hit" branch to keep in sync.

THREE GATES, in the order they run:
1. `faqSuggestionPopupEnabled` reads `hasFeature('faq_suggestion_popup')` --
   the client-visibility mechanism 0001/0002 already established via
   `window.__PROTON_CONFIG__.features` (`PROTON_FEATURES` at the Rails
   layer). This is a client-side convenience, exactly like `ai_assist`
   already is for the Copilot button, NOT the authoritative switch.
2. The confidence threshold above.
3. `dismissedFaqMessageId`: once dismissed, a suggestion for that exact
   message id never reopens, even if the component re-renders or the same
   `/kb/suggest` result comes back again on a later poll. A *new* customer
   message can surface a new suggestion.

KNOWN GAP, stated rather than engineered around: `FAQ_SUGGESTION_POPUP_ENABLED`
(the backend `Settings` field) and the tenant's `PROTON_FEATURES` list are
two independent switches today. `deploy/tenants/*.env`, `docker-compose.
tenant.yml` and `main.py` were all off-limits for this task, so nothing in
this patch or its backing work wires the backend flag into the frontend
runtime-config injection automatically -- an operator must add
`faq_suggestion_popup` to a tenant's `PROTON_FEATURES` for this strip to be
reachable at all, in addition to (not instead of) turning the backend
setting on. Recorded in the register and the operator handbook; closing it
is a deploy-config task, not a UI task, and was not invented here.

NOTE: hand-constructed, and NOT verified with `git apply --check` against a
real checkout -- this sandbox has no network access to clone upstream or the
fork, the same constraint recorded for patches 0053/0054/0055. This patch
stacks ON TOP OF 0002 AND 0055 (0055 itself stacks only on 0002): all five
hunks anchor on `ReplyTopPanel.vue` content those two patches themselves
already add (the `ref`/`computed` import, the `PROTON_ACTION_MODE` block,
the `hasFeature`/`showAiButton` setup block, the returned-identifiers list,
and the Translate button's closing `</div>`) -- never on unverified upstream
lines. Every context line here was transcribed verbatim from 0002's and
0055's own already-merged diffs (not from memory of unverified upstream
Chatwoot source), and the cumulative line-number arithmetic across both
parent patches plus this one was computed by a script, then verified for
real: the five hunks were diffed out of a synthetic before/after pair built
from that same transcribed content (padded with clearly-labelled filler for
the unknown surrounding lines, the same technique 0053 used), and applied
with a real `git apply` against a synthetic tree seeded with that base --
it applies cleanly and produces byte-identical output to the intended
after-file. That proves internal consistency and self-consistency with 0002
and 0055's own already-merged text only -- it does NOT prove this patch
applies to the real upstream-derived fork checkout, which this sandbox
cannot reach. If 0002 or 0055's actually-shipped content differs from what
is transcribed here, or a later patch also touches `ReplyTopPanel.vue`
